Article 3 The following construction projects conducted within the territory of the People's Republic of China, including the survey, design, construction, supervision of the projects and the procurement of key equipment and materials related to the construction, must be subject to tender:
(1) projects involving large-scale infrastructure, public utilities, and other matters that affect the public interest and public safety;
(2) projects wholly or partly invested with state-owned funds or financed by the state;
(3) projects using loans or assistance funds from international organizations or foreign governments.
The specific scope and scale standards for the projects listed in the preceding paragraph shall be formulated by the State Council's development planning department jointly with other relevant departments of the State Council, and shall be submitted to the State Council for approval.
Where laws or the State Council provide for the scope of other projects that must be subject to tender, such provisions shall be followed.

Article 41 The bid of the winning bidder shall meet one of the following conditions:
(1) being able to satisfy to the maximum extent the comprehensive evaluation standards specified in the tender documents;
(2) being able to meet the substantive requirements of the tender documents, and having the lowest evaluated bid price, except where the bid price is lower than the cost.
